      "message": "This is kind of tricky - the idea of `kIncompleteInput` (and even `kErrorInInput`) is that you got *some* good data. `SkCodec` subclasses are expected to set the remaining pixels to transparent black. If the result is `kIncompleteInput`, we could potentially get more data and finish the decode. (For `kErrorInInput`, there may be some valid data, but retrieving more input doesn\u0027t help.)\n\nDoesn\u0027t need to be fixed here, but maybe a `TODO`?",
